WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.336
-Republicans are rushing
to confirm

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.138
the Supreme Court nominee
of a president

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.274
who is in so much legal jeopardy
even his own lawyers

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.976
have warned him
he could go to jail.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.845
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer look.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:16.849
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:20.019
Let's just step back for
a moment and consider that fact

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.788
that Trump is trying
to appoint someone

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.990
to a lifetime seat
on the Supreme Court

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.892
while simultaneously
being implicated

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.427
in a truly staggering number
of criminal cases

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:29.695
and corruption scandals.

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:31.998
That's like Bonnie
getting arrested and saying,

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.766
"You know who's make
a great judge?

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:34.868
Clyde."

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.068
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:38.137
Just to review,
here's what we already know

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.306
about the various crimes
and corruption scandals

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.674
swirling around
the president --

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.142
his campaign chairman
was convicted

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:44.844
on eight counts
of tax and bank fraud,

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.079
his deputy campaign chairman

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.747
admitted to embezzlement
and money laundering,

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.749
his personal lawyer admitted
he conspired with the president

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.483
to break federal election laws
to pay hush money

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:52.685
to cover up an affair,

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.120
his national security adviser
plead guilty

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.122
to lying to the FBI about his
contacts with the Russians,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.057
his foreign policy adviser
also plead guilty

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.059
to lying to the FBI about
his contacts with the Russians,

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:01.227
his first
congressional backer

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.528
was indicted
for insider trading,

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.130
his second congressional backer
was indicted

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.066
for wire fraud
and campaign-finance violations,

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.733
a Republican lobbyist
just plead guilty

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.735
to steering illegal funds
from a pro-Russian oligarchy

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:10.904
to Trump's inauguration,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.572
and Steven Miller
has been sleeping rent-free

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:15.475
in the White House attic.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:18.211
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.678
Now...

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:20.880
[ Applause, laughter ]

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.883
...Trump's already --
already expressed support

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.217
for a few of those guys.

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.986
And now, he's backing
two more alleged criminals --

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:30.189
GOP congressmen Chris Collins
and Ducan Hunter.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.959
On Monday, Trump slammed
Attorney General Jeff Sessions

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.794
for allowing prosecutors
to bring cases against them.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.363
openly admitting that
those cases were hurting

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.298
Republicans' chances
in the midterm elections.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:42.067
-The president writes, quote,
"Two long-running, Obama era,

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.738
investigations of two very
popular Republican congressmen

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.541
were brought to a
well-publicized charge,

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.975
just ahead of
the midterms,

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:52.512
by the Jeff Sessions
Justice Department.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.780
Two easy wins
now in doubt

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.549
because there is
not enough time.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.983
Good job, Jeff."

00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:00.386
"The Democrats -- none of whom
voted for Jeff Sessions --

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.888
must love him now."

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.890
-First of all,
no one loves Jeff Sessions.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.524
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.059
He looks like
a haunted doll

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:09.796
that moves whenever
you look away.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:14.099
"I could have sworn I put my
Little Sessions of that chair.

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:15.935
Oh, my God,
he's behind me!"

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.104
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.506
Second --
think about that.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.374
Trump just openly admitted
on Twitter

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.775
that he wants
the Justice Department --

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.343
which is supposed
to be independent --

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:25.979
to cover up crimes
by Republicans

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.613
in order to help them
win elections.

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:30.249
Not only is Trump corrupt,
but he's so obvious about it.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:33.352
He's like a guy who would try to
pick your pocket from the front.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.521
[ As Trump ] "Whoops.
I've bumped into you by
accident.

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:39.058
now, just give me a second,
and I'll be on my way.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:42.862
Come on, wallet.
where are you, wallet."

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.463
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.465
[ Normal voice ]
In fact, today, we got
some explosive new details

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.268
about just how much
legal jeopardy

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.569
Trump's own lawyers
think he might be in.

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:53.238
Excerpts from famed journalist
Bob Woodward's forthcoming book

00:02:53.238 --> 00:02:55.241
about the Trump White House
began to leak out,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.276
including one conversation
where Trump's lawyer,

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:59.812
John Dowd, warned Trump
that if he testified

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.881
to the Russia probe,
he might go to jail.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.717
"Dowd was convinced that Trump
would commit perjury

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.953
if he talked to
Special Counsel Robert Mueller.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.420
But Trump,
concerned about the optics

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.222
of a president
refusing to testify,

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:12.258
and convinced that he could
handle Mueller's questions,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.960
had, by then,
decided otherwise.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.129
Trump told Dowd,
'I'll be a real good witness.'

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.499
Dowd replied,
'You are not a good witness.'"

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.603
In fact, the Mueller inquiry
apparently looms

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.372
over the White House every day,
to the point where

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.307
even foreign leaders
ask Trump about it.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:29.641
According to
the Washington Post,

00:03:29.641 --> 00:03:31.777
"Hovering over the White House
was Mueller's inquiry,

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.179
which deeply embarrassed
the president.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:35.681
Woodward describes Trump calling
his Egyptian counterpart

00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:38.251
to secure the release
of an imprisoned charity worker,

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.619
and President
Abdel Fatah al-Sissi saying,

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:42.655
'Donald, I'm worried about
this investigation.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.324
Are you going to be around?'

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.891
Trump relayed
the conversation to Dowd,

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:48.160
and said it was
'like a kick in the nuts.'"

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.530
In fairness, every day
working in your White House

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.398
is like a kick in the nuts.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.201
Why do you think Rudy Guiliani
always looks like this?

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:57.870
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.038
That's...

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.507
[ Applause ]

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.943
That's the face of a guy
who lost a bet

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.878
and has to stand in front of
a tennis-ball machine

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.146
without a racket.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.581
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:11.951
Apparently, Trump knew
this book would be explosive,

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:14.486
because last month he called
Woodward to talk about it.

00:04:14.486 --> 00:04:16.889
Woodward recorded the call,
and as he explained to Trump

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.924
what the book would be about,
you can hear it

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:22.995
slowly dawn on Trump that it
could be very damaging for him.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:28.500 line:0%
-It's also a difficult time,
where the political system,

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:31.337 line:0%
and you and my business...

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.406 line:0%
-Yeah.
-...is being tested.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:36.743 line:0%
-Yeah.
-And I take it very seriously.

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:39.111 line:0%
I've done books
on eight presidents,

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:41.747 line:0%
going back
from Nixon to Obama.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.350 line:0%
-Right.
-And I learned something

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.253 line:0%
about reporting, frankly,
Mr. President.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:50.923 line:0%
-Good.
-I've got to go talk to people,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:54.393 line:0%
and see them
outside of the White House,

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:56.428 line:0%
and outside
of their offices.

00:04:56.428 --> 00:05:01.034 line:0%
And I've gained a lot
of insight and documentation.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.302 line:0%
And it's -- you know,
it's a tough look

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:07.806 line:0%
at the world, and your
administration, and you.

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:09.442 line:0%
-Right. Well,
I assume that means

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.943 line:0%
it's gonna be
a negative book.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:11.978
-Oh, my God.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:15.181
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.082
He's like a guy
who doesn't understand

00:05:17.082 --> 00:05:18.417
why he's being dumped.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.853
"I'm breaking up with you
because you're dumb, annoying,

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.222
selfish, ugly,
and I don't like you,

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.525
and I'm not attracted to you
in any way."

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.526
[ As Trump ] "So, it sounds like
you're on the fence

00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:28.961
about going to prom with me."

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.497
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.731
[ Normal voice ] So, Trump
is harassing and threatening

00:05:32.731 --> 00:05:34.634
the Justice Department,
and even his own lawyers

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.935
have warned him
he might go to jail,

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:38.538
which is why it's absurd
to let him appoint anyone

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.773
to a permanent seat
on the Supreme Court,

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:42.642
let alone a life-long
partisan Republican

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.177
like Brett Kavanaugh.
And yet,

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.878
not only are Republicans
rushing forward

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.212
within Kavanaugh's nomination,

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:49.715
they're doing it with an
unprecedented level of secrecy.

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:51.883
"The Trump White House,
citing executive privilege,

00:05:51.883 --> 00:05:53.119
is withholding
from the Senate

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.920
more than 100,000
pages of records

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.121
from Kavanaugh's time
as a lawyer

00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:57.557
in the Bush
administration."

00:05:57.557 --> 00:06:00.326
Republicans are trying to hide
as much about Kavanaugh's record

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:02.328
as they can because they know
it would be damning.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:04.763
So, what do they want you to
know about Kavanaugh instead?

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:06.098
they want you to know that

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:08.267 line:0%
he's just like
your next-door neighbor.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.704 line:0%
-This is a guy
who coaches basketball,

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:15.107 line:0%
who does all kinds
of food pantries.

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:16.842 line:0%
He's like
your next-door neighbor.

00:06:16.842 --> 00:06:18.311 line:0%
-And then,
he talked about his daughter.

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:20.779 line:0%
And then, he talked about CYO
and food pantries.

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:24.183 line:0%
And I said, "You know what?
This is the guy next door."

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.051 line:0%
-Just a really nice guy.

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:28.920 line:0%
Just a decent person,
a person of integrity.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.556 line:0%
You have to see
his eyes light up

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:31.857 line:0%
when he talks
about his daughters,

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:33.492 line:0%
coaching their
basketball team.

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:38.230 line:0%
-One friend called him,
"A regular, old carpool dad."

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.533 line:0%
I think we all know
what that is.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:43.402 line:0%
It's the dad who drives
the kids to school.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:46.239
-[ Sarcastically ]
Oh, is that what it is?

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:49.241
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:54.013
The two words
with their exact definitions?

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:55.748
"He's like
a peanut-butter sandwich.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.149
We all know
what that is.

00:06:57.149 --> 00:06:59.886
It's a sandwich
with peanut butter on it."

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:01.720
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.289
And I'm sorry
you think he's qualified

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:06.292
to be a Supreme Court justice
because he's a carpool dad.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:08.460
Anyone can drive a car.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.295
Ruth Bader Ginsburg
pulled one

00:07:10.295 --> 00:07:13.666
when she wore -- when she won
World's Strongest Judge.

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:15.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.803
Now, today,
Democrats tried

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:19.605
to do everything they could
to delay the hearing

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.540
until all of Kavanaugh's
records were released.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.775
And the chairman
of the committee --

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:24.576
Iowa senator
Chuck Grassley --

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:26.445
did everything he could
to ignore them.

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:28.313
For example,
when several Democratic senators

00:07:28.313 --> 00:07:30.048
tried to interrupt
Grassley's opening statement

00:07:30.048 --> 00:07:32.751
to register their objections,
he just shouted over them.

00:07:32.751 --> 00:07:35.287 line:0%
-We cannot possibly
move forward, Mr. Chairman --

00:07:35.287 --> 00:07:37.523 line:0%
-I extend a very warm welcome...
-We have not been given...

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.192 line:0%
-...to Judge Kavanaugh...
-...an opportunity

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:40.892 line:0%
to have a meaningful hearing...
-...to his wife, Ashley...

00:07:40.892 --> 00:07:44.029 line:0%
-...on this nominee.
-...their two daughters...

00:07:44.029 --> 00:07:45.264 line:0%
-Mr. Chairman...
-...their extended family...

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.666 line:0%
-...I agree with my colleague...
-...and friends.

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:48.234 line:0%
-...Senator Harris.
Mr. Chairman...

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:51.604 line:0%
[ Indistinct talking,
interrupting ]

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:56.375
-You know you're not
in a good place

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:59.478
when you have to scream your
banal compliments at the
witness.

00:07:59.478 --> 00:08:01.847
[ Yelling ] "I want to
extend a very warm welcome

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:04.283
to your wife
and you two daughters!

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:06.485
I know that you are
a carpool dad --

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:09.322
which is a dad
who carpools!"

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:11.490
[ Scattered applause, laughter ]

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:15.294
[ Applause ]

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:16.662
[ Normal voice ]
Then...

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.430
when Senator Corey Booker
interrupted Grassley

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.265
to express his frustration
with the process,

00:08:20.265 --> 00:08:21.733
Grassley tried
a new tactic --

00:08:21.733 --> 00:08:24.604
ignoring Booker
and softly tapping his gavel.

00:08:24.604 --> 00:08:25.805 line:0%
-This committee, sir,

00:08:24.604 --> 00:08:25.805 line:14%
[ Gavel gently tapping ]

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:27.273 line:0%
is a violation
of even the values

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:30.009 line:0%
I've heard you talk about
time and time again,

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:31.243 line:0%
The ideals that
we should have.

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:32.712 line:0%
What is the rush?

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:33.946 line:0%
What are we
trying to hide

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:36.582 line:0%
by not having
the documents out front?

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:37.783 line:0%
What is with the rush?

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:37.783 line:14%
[ Gavel gently tapping ]

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:39.218 line:0%
What are we hiding
by not letting

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:40.886 line:0%
those documents
come out?

00:08:40.886 --> 00:08:42.721 line:0%
You've called for documents.

00:08:40.886 --> 00:08:42.721 line:14%
[ Gavel Gently tapping ]

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:44.256 line:0%
You yourself --
limited documents.

00:08:44.256 --> 00:08:45.657 line:0%
We thought there
should be more.

00:08:45.657 --> 00:08:47.459 line:0%
We have not
received the documents

00:08:47.459 --> 00:08:49.094 line:0%
that you have even called for.

00:08:47.459 --> 00:08:49.094 line:14%
[ Gavel gently tapping ]

00:08:49.094 --> 00:08:52.231
-Oh, my God. When Chuck Grassley
knocks on someone's door,

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:53.833
they probably don't even
know he's there.

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.235
"Chuck!
how long have you been here?"

00:08:57.235 --> 00:08:58.704
[ As Grassley ]
"Five hours."

00:08:58.704 --> 00:09:01.239
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.239 --> 00:09:02.774
[ Normal voice ]
When he tries to kill a fly,

00:09:02.774 --> 00:09:05.144
it probably
takes him forever.

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:08.047
[ Laughter ]

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:09.348
Is he calling for order

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:11.951
or trying to keep track
of his pulse?

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:14.353
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:15.854
Hey...

00:09:15.854 --> 00:09:18.057
Hey. Republicans say
we don't need to see

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:20.326
all of Kavanaugh's
records to confirm him
to the Supreme Court.

00:09:20.326 --> 00:09:21.593
And at least
they've been consistent.

00:09:21.593 --> 00:09:23.162
I'm sure there isn't
video of Grassley

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:25.531
from just a few years ago
saying the exact opposite

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:28.300
about President Obama's nominee
for the court, Elena Kagan.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:31.169 line:0%
